      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Reduction of indium boryl precursors to give two- and three-dimensional M-M bonded networks is influenced by the choice of supporting ligand. While the unprecedented nanoscale cluster [In68 (boryl)12 ]- (with an In12 @In44 @In12 (boryl)12 concentric structure), can be isolated from the potassium reduction of a bis(boryl)indium(III) chloride precursor, analogous reduction of the corresponding (benzamidinate)InIII Br(boryl) system gives a near-planar (and weakly aromatic) tetranuclear [In4 (boryl)4 ]2- system."
      },
